                                            </div>
                                            <div class="col-sm-6 col-md-4 col-lg-3">
                                                <button class="btn default search-tag " type="button" data-tag="sci_fi" data-label="Sci-fi" data-tooltip aria-haspopup="true" data-disable-hover="false" tabindex="1" title="Science fiction stories take place in imaginative, futuristic settings. Common elements include space travel, advanced technology, time travel, parallel universes, and extraterrestrial life.">
                                                        <input type="hidden" name="" value="sci_fi"/>
                                                    <span class="tag-label" data-tagname="Sci-fi">
                                                        Sci-fi
                                                    </span>
                                                </button>
                                            </div>
                                            <div class="col-sm-6 col-md-4 col-lg-3">
                                                <button class="btn default search-tag " type="button" data-tag="one_shot" data-label="Short Story" data-tooltip aria-haspopup="true" data-disable-hover="false" tabindex="1" title="Short stories are pieces intended to be read in one sitting. Because of its condensed form, short stories often have brief or skipped introductions, as well as open-ended or abrupt conclusions. Plot is condensed, and these stories are less complex than full novels.">
                                                        <input type="hidden" name="" value="one_shot"/>
                                                    <span class="tag-label" data-tagname="Short Story">
                                                        Short Story
                                                    </span>
                                                </button>
                                            </div>
                                            <div class="col-sm-6 col-md-4 col-lg-3">
                                                <button class="btn default search-tag " type="button" data-tag="thriller" data-label="Thriller" data-tooltip aria-haspopup="true" data-disable-hover="false" tabindex="1" title="Stories that focus on suspense and high-stakes, plot-driven narratives.">
                                                        <input type="hidden" name="" value="thriller"/>
                                                    <span class="tag-label" data-tagname="Thriller">
                                                        Thriller
                                                    </span>
                                                </button>
                                            </div>
                                            <div class="col-sm-6 col-md-4 col-lg-3">
                                                <button class="btn default search-tag " type="button" data-tag="tragedy" data-label="Tragedy" data-tooltip aria-haspopup="true" data-disable-hover="false" tabindex="1" title="Tragedy is a form of drama that invokes human suffering. Classic tragic stories are intended to provide cartharsis, or purging of negative emotion in the audience. Stories involve a noble character brought low by fate or circumstance.">
                                                        <input type="hidden" name="" value="tragedy"/>
                                                    <span class="tag-label" data-tagname="Tragedy">
                                                        Tragedy
                                                    </span>
                                                </button>
                                            </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <label>Additional Tags</label>
                                    <div class="row">
                                        <div class="col-xs-12">
                                            <label>Only include matching all tags:</label>
                                            <div class="form-group">
                                                <select name="tagsAdd" multiple class="tomselect">
                                                            <option data-description="Anti-Hero Lead stories depict leading characters that lack the usual heroic qualities such as idealism, courage, or morality. Usually, anti-heroes blur the lines between a hero and a villain, depicting the characteristics of both." value="anti-hero_lead">Anti-Hero Lead</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories featuring characters who take on the role of the villain but retain sympathetic, moral, or understandable motives." value="antivillain_lead">Anti-Villain Lead</option>
                                                            <option data-description="The main character&#x27;s home world, universe, or equivalent, faces the threat of imminent destruction, and the main character is working to stop it or survive through it." value="apocalypse">Apocalypse</option>
                                                            <option data-description="A subgenre focusing on characters or major actors that are advanced AI.&#xD;&#xA;" value="artificial_intelligence">Artificial Intelligence</option>
                                                            <option data-description="The main character of this novel is exceptionally attractive - to the point where it deserves an extra tag on the story due to the sheer significance." value="attractive_lead">Attractive Lead</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories that focus on themes of family loyalty, honor, upright honesty, integrity, and chivalry.&#xD;&#xA;" value="chivalry">Chivalry</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Multiple characters are vying for the MC&#x27;s attention, but the MC will only choose one." value="competing_love">Competing Love Interest</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories that give the reader a feeling of warmth, comfort, and relaxation, with minimal stress or conflict.&#xD;&#xA;" value="cozy">Cozy</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories that center around the creation, refinement, and mastery of items, potions, artifacts, or other crafted works.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;" value="crafting">Crafting</option>
                                                            <option data-description="A type of Chinese martial arts novel that typically focuses on cultivation and a quest for immortality." value="cultivation">Cultivation</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Cyberpunk is a subgenre of science fiction that focuses on technological advancements themselves. They usually feature a change of social order because of said advancements." value="cyberpunk">Cyberpunk</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories set in worlds where power systems revolve around cards, where characters gain abilities or strength based on the cards they possess." value="deck_building">Deck Building</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories focus on a sentient dungeon or an entity that controls one." value="dungeon_core">Dungeon Core</option>
                                                            <option data-description="A type of fiction that takes place or focuses on loot-bearing Dungeons similar to the eponymous RPG." value="dungeon_crawler">Dungeon Crawler</option>
                                                            <option data-description="A society where the common person&#x27;s living conditions are undesirable or frightening, often with a totalitarian government/authority." value="dystopia">Dystopia</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Female Lead stories have, unsurprisingly, a leading female human character, or of any particular sapient humanoid race." value="female_lead">Female Lead</option>
                                                            <option data-description=" A story focusing on the first meeting between two or more species or societies and the events that occur because of it.&#xD;&#xA;" value="first_contact">First Contact</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Novels set in game-like worlds of any game genre. Does not need to heavily focus on visual statistics." value="gamelit">GameLit</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Gender Bender fictions utilise the theme of gender swapping. The gender swapping can be temporary or permanent, full or partial, and may or may not be the theme based on which the fiction revolves." value="gender_bender">Gender Bender</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Characters are genetically modified to be superior to their original species." value="genetically_engineered">Genetically Engineered </option>
                                                            <option data-description="Grimdark is a subgenre or a way to describe the tone, style or setting of speculative fiction (especially fantasy) that is, depending on the definition used, markedly dystopian or amoral, or particularly violent or realistic." value="grimdark">Grimdark</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Uses theoretically possible science and attempts to explain how the science works; does not include fantasy elements." value="hard_sci-fi">Hard Sci-fi</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Defined by its epic nature, High Fantasy takes place in an alternate world with its own rules and laws." value="high_fantasy">High Fantasy</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories where the main character is focused on building a long-standing base, usually a kingdom or an equivalent" value="kingdom_building">Kingdom Building</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories that include characters who are interested in or pursuing lesbian relationships." value="lesbian_romance">Lesbian Romance</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Novels where linear progression, such as levels, are main themes of the story. Almost always shows stat boxes, EXP gain, and other notifications." value="litrpg">LitRPG</option>
                                                            <option data-description="A character born and raised within their own world and time. They possess no external knowledge beyond their world, and that world has not undergone any drastic, unpredictable changes. The character&#x2019;s understanding is limited to what they learn within the confines of their own reality." value="local_protagonist">Local Protagonist</option>
                                                            <option data-description="A type of fantasy that takes place in the real world, putting fantastical elements in an otherwise natural setting." value="low_fantasy">Low Fantasy</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Magic fictions contain the use or means of magic (as charms or spells) that have supernatural power over natural forces. Practitioners are commonly referred to as mages (or magi), witches and warlocks, wizards, and sorcerers. Most commonly used in fantasy fictions." value="magic">Magic</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories where an ordinary person (usually a young girl) is granted magical powers and a mission, often involving battles against monsters unseen by the ordinary world." value="magical_girl">Magical Girl</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories where magic and technology are combined, where technology produces magical effects and/or is powered by magic.&#xD;&#xA;" value="magitech">Magitech</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories that include characters who are interested in or pursuing gay(male) relationships.&#xD;&#xA;" value="gay_romance">Male Gay Romance</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Male Lead stories have, you guessed it, a leading male human character, or of any particular sapient humanoid race." value="male_lead">Male Lead</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Martial Arts stories commonly describe to great detail the intricacies of western or eastern combat." value="martial_arts">Martial Arts</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories featuring giant piloted robots, usually (but not always) humanoid in shape.&#xD;&#xA;" value="mecha">Mecha</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories where the main character uses knowledge from modern Earth, another world, or a future timeline to advance a less-developed society.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;" value="modern_knowledge">Modern Knowledge</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories where the protagonist begins life as a monster, beast, or non-human creature and grows stronger through evolution." value="monster_evolution">Monster Evolution</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Multiple Lead Characters fictions depict stories said from points of view of a number of characters, the actual number varying between two and too many to count. The characters can be of any gender and race." value="multiple_lead">Multiple Lead Characters</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Multiple Lovers (previously Harem) stories depict multiple characters who have romantic interest toward the lead. Sometimes, it includes polyamorous relationships." value="harem">Multiple Lovers</option>
                                                            <option data-description="A type of fiction focusing on mythology, such as deities and elements of the divine, or the occult." value="mythos">Mythos</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Non-Human Lead stories have main character(s) not be human, whether partially or completely. The term may include or exclude humanoid fantastical races. The main theme of said stories can be the loss or redefinition of the term human or humane." value="non-human_lead">Non-Human Lead</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories where the main character is not humanoid. They are NOT human, nor elf/dwarf, or any other near-human species.&#xA0;.&#xA0;" value="nonhumanoid_lead">Non-Humanoid Lead</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories where a character (usually female) enters the world of a game or novel and tries to avoid a bad ending.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;" value="otome">Otome</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Features a fantastical world that is entered through a portal or some other means, and differs from the real world. In Japan, this type of work is known as isekai (different world)." value="summoned_hero">Portal Fantasy / Isekai</option>
                                                            <option data-description="The world has been ruined, and this is the story of the survivors." value="post_apocalyptic">Post Apocalyptic</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Characters work to improve themselves over time rather than acquiring rapid growth, usually through training, grinding, studying, and/or introspection." value="progression">Progression</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Reader Interactive uses reader inputs (usually polls) to define the progression of the novel. They can also be &#x201C;choose your own adventure&#x201D; stories, told in second person narrative." value="reader_interactive">Reader Interactive</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Reincarnation utilises a common theme of a person&#x27;s life restarting or beginning anew after their death, not necessarily connected to the teachings of hinduism and buddhism." value="reincarnation">Reincarnation</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories with romance as a subplot, the driving factor of the story isn&#x27;t romance." value="romance">Romance Subplot</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Royalty, nobles, or characters in a body of governance, playing a major part in the story. Typically involving a power struggle. " value="ruling_class">Ruling Class</option>
                                                            <option data-description="School Life stories usually place their characters in a setting regarding education and schooling. The main character(s) are usually students in the institutions. School Life may be a primary theme, or can just span a portion of the story." value="school_life">School Life</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Secret Identity fictions use the theme of subterfuge and secrecy employed by one or more characters (main or otherwise) to pose as different personae. The secret identity is usually vital to the story or setting." value="secret_identity">Secret Identity</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Slice of Life stories usually depict snippets or parts of one or more characters&#x2019; life, which may or may not be connected to the main plot themselves. There doesn&#x2019;t even have to be a main plot in a traditional sense." value="slice_of_life">Slice of Life</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Uses futuristic-type science, but doesn&#x27;t explain how the technology works and the science isn&#x2019;t necessarily realistic or feasible" value="soft_sci-fi">Soft Sci-fi</option>
                                                            <option data-description="A subgenre of science fiction that focuses on space warfare, interplanetary battles, futuristic weapons, and is usually set in outer space. May include subthemes of chivalry and romance." value="space_opera">Space Opera</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Sports fictions focus on competitive displays of physical or mental prowess. The sports can be real or imaginary, but usually have to contain a self-explanatory set of rules." value="sports">Sports</option>
                                                            <option data-description="A subgenre of science fiction inspired by and incorporating 19th-century industrial steam-powered machinery and technology, usually set in an alternate Victorian Era or the Wild West." value="steampunk">Steampunk</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Strategy stories depict characters or setting that do not rely on pure physical prowess, combat, or clashing, instead depicting tactical and critical thinking." value="strategy">Strategy</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Strong Lead stories depict characters which are unnaturally or unusually potent compared to the norm of the setting they are in. They can be either physically and/or mentally superior, or have a different advantage altogether." value="strong_lead">Strong Lead</option>
                                                            <option data-description="A subgenre focusing on people with supernatural abilities, or ones that focus on fighting the evil of the universe, usually in costumes." value="super_heroes">Super Heroes</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Supernatural stories contain an unnatural element which cannot be found in reality. Common themes include magic, zombies, vampires, werewolves, dragons, and other fae. Supernatural fictions are usually alternate world or low fiction stories, where the main setting is in the actual contemporary Earth." value="supernatural">Supernatural</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories that focus on the character&#x2019;s struggle to survive." value="survival">Survival</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories where a game-like System appears in the main character&#x2019;s world, often accompanied by the arrival of magic, monsters, and the collapse of modern technology." value="system_invasion">System Invasion</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Characters are enhanced or created through technology, such as cyborgs or robots.&#xD;&#xA;" value="technologically_engineered">Technologically Engineered</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Characters relive the same time period through a loop; may or may not involve alternate timelines." value="loop">Time Loop</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Characters directly travel through time, possibly within the same timeline, alternate timelines, or even creating new timelines." value="time_travel">Time Travel</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Stories centered around towers that must be climbed to survive. These towers are often filled with challenges, monsters, and rewards.&#xD;&#xA;" value="tower">Tower</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Works that feature fantastical or supernatural elements in an urban setting, which may or may not be contemporary." value="urban_fantasy">Urban Fantasy</option>
                                                            <option data-description="As opposed to Anti-Hero, villain leads are not benevolent. Usually features protagonists with immoral or evil goals." value="villainous_lead">Villainous Lead</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Virtual Reality stories often incorporate headsets or full-body machines that simulate a different reality or depict moving a human consciousness entirely into a virtual or digital environment. The story can span both the actual and the virtual reality." value="virtual_reality">Virtual Reality</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Fictions that focus on war and the military life of soldiers." value="war_and_military">War and Military</option>
                                                            <option data-description="Based on Chinese literature wuxia (Martial Heroes) features itinerant warriors of ancient China, often depicted as capable of superhuman feats of martial arts." value="wuxia">Wuxia</option>
                                                </select>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
