                        <div class="col-sm-6 uppercase bold font-blue-dark">
                            <i class="fa fa-list" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            <span>14 Chapters</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-sm-6 uppercase bold font-blue-dark">
                            <i class="fa fa-calendar" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            <time unixtime="1791748812" title="Sunday, October 11, 2026 8:00:12&#x202F;PM" datetime="2026-10-11T20:00:12.0000000&#x2B;00:00" format="U" dateonly="true">Sunday, October 11, 2026 8:00:12&#x202F;PM</time>
                        </div>
                        <div id="description-195767" class="margin-top-10 col-xs-12" style="display: none; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word">
                            <p><strong>Eric's the only one in the System apocalypse. Downside? Lonely. Upside: He gets <em>all</em> the loot.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p>
<p>Left alone on a demolished Earth after the System apocalypse wipes nearly all of civilization's creations off the map, Eric, skipped by the Tutorial, finds himself the first (and only) person to face the World Dungeon the System is shaping the planet into. Forget a difficult tutorial; with no tutorial at all, he's in the deep end, thrust directly into hell difficulty. What's an office drone engineer and former coffee gofer to do but level up, clear dungeons, and grow as strong as he can in order to best the Great Game?&nbsp;</p>
<p>Not only that, but it turns out the Tutorial might not be as kind and helpful as he hoped. Given glimpses of the Tutorial, Eric quickly realizes that it's wildly inadequate, meant to spit out fodder for the Game to chew up for the delight of the faceless audience. Setting humanity up for failure? Not on his watch.</p>
<p>The Great Game is the greatest entertainment the universe has ever seen, and that means it's livestreamed. The Tutorial is livestreamed, the dungeons are livestreamed... and so is Eric. Given the largest platform imaginable, Eric sets forth to help his fellow humans by creating <em>The Practical Guide to Solo Dungeoneering</em>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>But it's not going to be easy. The universe's viewers are mysterious, and the Great Game itself is full of thorns--and did he mention the hell difficulty? Eric's got his work cut out for him. And he's going to cut it down to size and send it back out into the world in manageable, comprehensible bites.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Dungeon Crawler Carl meets Solo Leveling meets Omniscient Reader's Viewpoint, with a little bit of Steve Irwin thrown in for flavor.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<p>TLDR:&nbsp;</p>
<p>-Mage MC</p>
<p>-Dungeon Crawling SysApoc</p>
<p>-Weak to strong / progression</p>
<p>-Skills, spells, and lots of loot</p>
<p>-A dungeon guide (eventually)&nbsp;</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
