                        <div id="description-146285" class="margin-top-10 col-xs-12" style="display: none; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word">
                            <div>
<p><br>Gnash spent ten years in the character creation lobby optimizing the perfect solo build.</p>
<p>Then he got isekai'd into a permadeath server, accidentally Soulbound to two strangers, and forced into a "Holy Trinity Challenge" that requires a Tank, Healer, and DPS to clear every dungeon as a trio in order... or die.</p>
<p>His party:<br>A kleptomaniac gambler whose class is literally a slot machine, and an unstoppable seven-foot cow-woman bliss ninny who sees everything through G-rated filters and lectures raid bosses about using their inside voices and keeps rattling off streamer bait for lonely subscribers in a world where there are none.&nbsp;</p>
<p>They call her "Yllana Wolf. Yllana the Typhoon. The Bovinoid Stampede."</p>
<p>She's a one cow stampede.&nbsp;</p>
<p>A LitRPG comedy about min-maxing, market manipulation, and the terrifying power of aggressive delusional positivity.</p>
<p>What to expect:<br>- Mild to spicy existential horror<br>- Simulated violence<br>- Aggressive capitalism<br>- One (1) cow who doesn't know she's a cow or alive<br>- Emotional damage disguised as comedy<br>- No romance, no sex, no weird freaky shit</p>
<p>Comps:</p>
<p>- Some kinda The Greatest Estate Developer: Scummy protagonist, comedy, competence porn<br>- Solo Leveling (if the hero was forced to party and hated every second of "trio leveling")&nbsp;<br>- Bofuri - &nbsp;Accidental OP builds, but with more crying<br>- Log Horizon - Trapped MMO, economics matter, but funnier and sadder</p>
<p><em>&nbsp;</em></p>
</div>
