                        <div id="description-194531" class="margin-top-10 col-xs-12" style="display: none; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word">
                            <p>Fanfiction, Solo Leveling, but Jiwoo isn't the main character, Joohee is receiving the system instead&nbsp;</p>
<p></p>
<p>Joohee Lee gave everything she had to keep her raid alive. When her legs finally gave out inside the Double Dungeon, she begged Sung Jinwoo and Song Chi-Yul to leave while they still could.</p>
<p>They escaped, and she stayed behind instead of Jinwoo&nbsp;</p>
<p>She wakes in a hospital with her wounds gone and a strange blue window floating beside her bed. The System has chosen her as its Player, granting her something hunters are never supposed to have: the ability to keep growing stronger.</p>
<p>Joohee wants to restore what her friends lost and become strong enough to bring everyone home. Every completed quest takes her closer, and the punishment for failure makes her next deadline a matter of survival.</p>
<p>Then her magic starts following hunters home.</p>
<p>Buffs linger long after the raid ends. Fresh injuries close on people she healed hours earlier. When an unexpected surge of power reaches Cha Hae-In, the S-rank swordswoman begins searching for the healer responsible.</p>
<p>As curiosity grows into trust and something more, Joohee finds herself wanting to share a secret she barely understands. Meanwhile, the System is offering her abilities that could let her clear entire dungeons alone.</p>
<p>Joohee has spent her life learning how to heal.</p>
<p>She is about to discover how dangerous that power can become.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
