                        <div id="description-192219" class="margin-top-10 col-xs-12" style="display: none; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word">
                            <p><strong>Apex Ascension</strong></p>
<p><em>An Apex Force × Solo Leveling Crossover</em></p>
<p>Sambulo "Sam" Zuma just wanted a quiet run.</p>
<p>Nineteen years old, Vice-Captain of Alpha Squad, half Wolf and half Dragon — Sam has spent the last year fighting monsters the size of buildings and outrunning lightning for a living. So when he takes the Wolf Path alone to clear his head, the last thing he expects is to get ripped off course entirely and dropped onto Floor 79 of a hundred-floor Demon Castle in a world that isn't his own.</p>
<p>He clears the floor before he even finds the stairs.</p>
<p>Sung Jinwoo — the weakest E-Rank Hunter alive, three years into a war nobody believes he can win — arrives to find his floor already cleared, and a stranger with glowing blue eyes sitting on a boulder like he owns the place. Neither of them planned on a partner. Both of them are about to need one.</p>
<p>Together they'll climb what's left of the Castle, face down a Demon Monarch, and walk straight into the ant-infested nightmare of Jeju Island — where Sam's silver fire and Jinwoo's growing shadow army will be tested against threats neither world was built to handle alone.</p>
<p>But power doesn't stay still. Sam has a ceiling. Jinwoo doesn't.</p>
<p><em>A crossover about two soldiers from two different kinds of war — and what happens when one of them starts outgrowing the other.</em></p>
<p>This is a crossover featuring my original character Sambulo Zuma and the Apex Force power system. If you enjoyed Sam and the Nova system, the main series Apex Force is ongoing on my profile</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
